Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Topology/SpernerGrid.lean-29-/-- An edge whose ends carry labels `x` and `y` is a *door* when one label is `0` and the other `1`;
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Topology/SpernerGrid.lean-30-the indicator, valued in `ZMod 2` because only the parity of the door count matters. -/
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Topology/SpernerGrid.lean-31-def door (x y : Fin 3) : ZMod 2 :=
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Topology/SpernerGrid.lean-32-  if (x = 0 ∧ y = 1) ∨ (x = 1 ∧ y = 0) then 1 else 0
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Topology/SpernerGrid.lean-33-
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Topology/SpernerGrid.lean-34-/-- Three labels are *rainbow* when they are pairwise distinct, i.e. `{x, y, z} = {0, 1, 2}`. -/
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Topology/SpernerGrid.lean:35:def Rainbow (x y z : Fin 3) : Prop :=
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Topology/SpernerGrid.lean-36-  x ≠ y ∧ y ≠ z ∧ x ≠ z
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Topology/SpernerGrid.lean-37-
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Topology/SpernerGrid.lean-38-/-- `Rainbow` is decided label by label. -/
