### HadwigerNelson.Thomassen.IsTwoSep
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Thomassen.lean-35-def offTwo (x y : V) : Set V := {v | v ≠ x ∧ v ≠ y}
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Thomassen.lean-36-
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Thomassen.lean-37-/-- **`int(G, x, y)`** (CVB B2 step 2, in place of Thomassen's curve `R`): the vertices of the finite connected components of `G − x − y`. -/
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Thomassen.lean-38-def twoSepInterior (x y : V) : Set V :=
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Thomassen.lean-39-  {v | ∃ hv : v ∈ offTwo x y, ((G.induce (offTwo x y)).connectedComponentMk ⟨v, hv⟩).supp.Finite}
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Thomassen.lean-40-
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Thomassen.lean-41-/-- **A 2-separator** `{x, y}`: two distinct vertices whose removal leaves a finite component. -/
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Thomassen.lean:42:def IsTwoSep (x y : V) : Prop := x ≠ y ∧ (twoSepInterior G x y).Nonempty
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Thomassen.lean-43-
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Thomassen.lean-44-/-- **A maximal 2-separator** (`[Thomassen1999]` p. 852): a 2-separator `{x, y}` such that no 2-separator `{u, v}` has `x` or `y` in its
Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Thomassen.lean-45-interior. -/
